[Music]  our latest cbs news battleground tracker  poll finds president trump  behind in two states he is targeting for  victory  democratic nominee joe biden has a nine  point lead in minnesota  which the president came close to  winning in 2016  and biden is three points ahead in  arizona where the president campaigns  today  in our poll half of registered arizona  voters say  biden would do a better job handling the  corona virus  nancy cordes has been talking to voters  there all weekend and joins us from  tempe nancy what are voters telling you  well anthony they're telling us that  they are angry  and that while president trump won this  state  four years ago the pandemic is now  really shaping the race  in 2020 and in fact voters who say that  they've been  financially impacted by the virus were  far more likely to say  they're ready for a change  in phoenix from outdoor cafes  to hiking trails to the golf course  one issue kept coming up most biggest  concern to everybody certainly in my age  group  is health coronavirus  arizona is still recovering from a  massive summer spike  more than 2 000 deaths in july alone so  in our battleground tracker we asked  arizona voters  who would do a better job handling the  pandemic  they gave former vice president joe  biden a 13-point edge  i think anybody would do a better job  than donald trump to be honest with you  sherry tackett is a nurse practitioner i  felt like he was ignoring all the advice  and firing people that were giving him  good advice  82 percent of arizona republicans said  the trump administration is doing  all it can i don't know if anybody has  the real recipe to it  i think he could have done way better  federico lemon-meyer is a reluctant  trump supporter i think he's done many  wrong things but i think it's despite  the the  of that i think the country is going in  the right direction  oh yeah yes this is what campaigning  looks like in the covid era  we got some great conversations with the  people we caught up with one group that  only recently started canvassing again  with protective gear we knew that we had  we needed to turn out people and the  best way to do it is to have direct  conversations with them so  we decided we're going to get load up on  ppe face masks face shields and still go  out and talk to people  and what kind of reception do you get  are people afraid to open the door right  now  um actually they're more intrigued it  seems like with the protection that we  have on  there they want to know what we're doing  vice president biden  hasn't been to the state in person all  year  while republicans are taking a different  tack getting ready to welcome  mr trump to the state today for the  fifth time this year is it safe  for the president to travel here and  hold events it's very safe  the virus is just one reason this  reliably red  state is suddenly up for grabs i'm a  older white republican male who is  voting because of morality  not just policy and  i can't i can't vote for trump i just  think he's a crook  i think he is everything i don't want in  office tensions over the race  are riding high i've lost friends really  yes i've lost friends because of that we  met the murray skull family  after mass in downtown phoenix they made  up their minds  long ago trump yes why  because it's pro-life and i can argue  about racism but i can argue about life  that's a non-negotiable issue that's  negotiable for us and then there's  patricia matheus  a teacher i don't understand how latin  people can  like him now like 62 percent of the  latinos in our arizona poll  she plans to vote against mr trump i  think it's too much hate in that  latinos make up 30 percent of this  state's population and their numbers  have grown  since 2016. arizona has also seen  an influx of california residents  seeking jobs  and a lower cost of living all of that  and more has put the state's 11  electoral votes in play and there is a  real chance tony that this state  could go for the democrat for president  for the first time  since 1996. wow that's a great piece  nancy polls are one thing but i love  hearing from voters so we appreciate  that

